LU5400 CM12.1 RIL and modem GPS compatibility
============================================

native/ is based on the unchanged local CM12.1 hardware/ril/libril sources.
LU540141 request/response layouts come from the CM11 device implementation
(commit 5208258); the proprietary lge-ril.so modem implementation is retained.
The source transport keeps CM12.1 standard parcel encodings and version
fallbacks. LG call records use a 32-bit isVoice; GET_IMSI, DEACTIVATE_DATA_CALL
and DTMF_START use the verified LG layouts. Private request handlers retain
stock allocation lifetimes where modem ownership has not been established.

CM12.1 standard requests 109..131 are unsupported by this old modem and
return REQUEST_NOT_SUPPORTED. The last standard request is
SET_RADIO_CAPABILITY (131); LG private 134 and later entries retain their
original numeric table positions. They must not be shifted by a newer
platform header or an omitted hole in the table.
The Java P2RIL class preserves its configured name but does not send P940
XMM commands. LG notifications 1038..1094 are not interpreted as Lollipop
standard events; their unimplemented framework semantics are still a limit.

Raw LU540141 inputs remain in vendor/lge/lu5400/proprietary. fixup_ril.py
accepts only their exact SHA-256 hashes and verifies ELF segments, relocation
layout and all original destructor instructions. It changes the single CRT
absolute __dso_handle literal into a PC-relative calculation and removes only
its now-unnecessary relocation and TEXTREL flag. Runtime algorithms and all
other relocations remain unchanged. There is no non-PIE linker exception.
rild is built as a normal PIE executable; libril is built from source.

The stock GPS HAL is a shared library using MDM6600 channel /dev/pts9.
It replaces the mismatched Broadcom daemon/frontend path. The modem itself
uses /dev/ttyspi3 and the stock ipc_channels.config. File contexts map actual
modem nodes to existing radio_device and gps_device types; no new allow rule
or permissive setting is added. A rebuilt boot ramdisk is needed to persist
ueventd/file_contexts changes across a kernel reboot.

Reference comparison: CyanogenMod omap4-common b67054f69f8b463f026abeb6a205ac0f5ae9e9f8
rejects unsupported older-modem commands at the device boundary. Motorola GPS
wrapper 008913668adc2da7f836f0f5c679d0d935eac1ef (and follow-up 0bbb95c)
fixes a signed pthread_t check; LU540141's inspected init ignores that callback
return value, so that wrapper is not copied. Motorola modem blobs/IPC are not
interchangeable with the LU540141 LG implementation.
